## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to build a dynamic, per-tenant UI with streaming data, memoization, and lazy loading, plus robust error handling and lifecycle on tenant changes.

## Key Concepts

- useSyncExternalStore for streaming manifests
- memoized selectors keyed by (tenantId, dashboardId, version)
- React.lazy and Suspense for dynamic widgets
- Error boundaries and per-widget isolation
- subscription lifecycle on tenant switch

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton: memoized selector for widgets
function createWidgetSelector() {
  const cache = new Map();
  return (tenantId, dashboardId, version, widgets) => {
    const key = `${tenantId}:${dashboardId}:${version}`;
    if (!cache.has(key)) {
      cache.set(key, widgets.map(w => w.type)); // simplified
    }
    return cache.get(key);
  };
}
```

